“(7) After comparing the violation photos recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment with the motor vehicle information registered in the road traffic violation information management system, it is confirmed that the recorded motor vehicle license plate information is incorrect;
“(8) Other circumstances that should be eliminated.”
7. Add one article as Article 23: “If verified to be true, photos or videos of violations provided by a unit or individual may be used as evidence for punishment.
“The audit and entry requirements for photos or videos of violations reported by the public shall be implemented with reference to these provisions.”
8. Change Article 23 to Article 25 and revise it as follows: “When implementing the administrative coercive measures specified in items (1), (2), (4), and (5) of Article 24 of these provisions, the following procedures shall be followed:
“(1) Orally inform the violator or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle of the basic facts of the violation, the type, basis, and rights they enjoy according to law regarding the administrative coercive measure to be taken;
“(2) Listen to the statements and defenses of the party; if the facts, reasons, or evidence raised by the party are valid, they shall be adopted;
“(3) Prepare an administrative coercive measure voucher and inform the party to go to the designated location for processing within fifteen days;
“(4) The administrative coercive measure voucher shall be signed by the party and signed or stamped by the traffic police, and stamped with the seal of the public security organ traffic management department; if the party refuses to sign, the traffic police shall note it on the administrative coercive measure voucher;
“(5) The administrative coercive measure voucher shall be delivered to the party on the spot; if the party refuses to accept it, the traffic police shall note it on the administrative coercive measure voucher, which shall constitute service.
“When administrative coercive measures are taken on the spot, the traffic police shall report to the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department to which they belong within twenty-four hours and complete the approval procedures. If the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department considers that administrative coercive measures should not be taken, they shall be immediately lifted.”
9. Change Article 33 to Article 35 and revise it as follows: “If a vehicle driver has any of the following circumstances, the alcohol content in their body shall be tested:
“(1) They object to the alcohol content result tested by methods such as alcohol breath testing and raise the objection on the spot;
“(2) A traffic accident occurs involving a vehicle suspected of drunk driving;
“(3) They are suspected of drunk driving;
“(4) They refuse to cooperate with testing by methods such as alcohol breath testing.
“If a vehicle driver has no objection to the alcohol breath test result, they shall sign to confirm. Objections raised afterward shall not be accepted.
“If a vehicle driver is suspected of driving a vehicle after taking, injecting drugs, or taking state-controlled psychotropic drugs or narcotic drugs, they shall be tested for drug use in accordance with the “Provisions on Drug Testing Procedures,” and their family members shall be notified, except when notification is impossible.
“For those who are out of control due to drinking or drug use or refuse to cooperate with inspection or testing, restrictive police equipment such as restraint belts or warning ropes may be used.”
10. Change Article 34 to Article 36 and revise it as follows: “When testing the alcohol content in a vehicle driver’s body, the following procedures shall be followed:
“(1) Two traffic police officers, or one traffic police officer leading auxiliary police personnel, shall take the vehicle driver to a medical institution to extract a blood sample, or a blood sample shall be extracted on the spot by personnel with corresponding qualifications such as forensic doctors;
“(2) The public security organ traffic management department shall send the blood sample to a unit or institution with testing qualifications for testing within five days after extracting the blood sample, and shall inform the vehicle driver of the test results in writing within five days after receiving the test results.
“When testing the alcohol content in a vehicle driver’s body, their family members shall be notified, except when notification is impossible.
“If a vehicle driver objects to the test results, they may apply for a retest within three days from the date of receiving the test results.
“A retest shall be conducted under any of the following circumstances:
“(1) The testing procedure is illegal or violates relevant professional technical requirements, which may affect the correctness of the test results;
“(2) The testing unit or institution, or the tester, does not have the corresponding qualifications and conditions;
“(3) The test results are obviously insufficiently supported;
“(4) The tester intentionally conducts a false test;
“(5) The tester should have recused themselves but did not;
“(6) The test sample is false or contaminated;
“(7) Other circumstances that require a retest.
“If the circumstances specified in the preceding paragraph are not met, upon approval by the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department at or above the county level, a decision shall be made not to grant a retest, and the applicant shall be notified in writing within three days from the date of the decision.
“For a retest, the public security organ shall separately assign or hire a tester.”
11. Change Article 41 to Article 43 and revise it as follows: “For a violation punished with a warning or a fine of not more than 200 yuan, the simplified procedure may apply.
“For a violation punished with a fine of more than 200 yuan (excluding 200 yuan), temporary detention or revocation of a motor vehicle driver’s license, the general procedure shall apply. If no administrative coercive measures are needed, the on-site traffic police shall collect and fix relevant evidence and prepare a violation processing notice. Among them, for a violation punished solely with a fine of more than 200 yuan (excluding 200 yuan), it may be handled quickly through measures such as simplified evidence collection methods and examination and approval procedures.
“For a violation punished with administrative detention, it shall be implemented in accordance with the “Provisions of Public Security Organs on Handling Administrative Cases.””
