Article 18 The records of illegal acts collected by traffic technical monitoring equipment used as the basis for handling shall clearly and accurately reflect the type, license plate, appearance and other characteristics of the motor vehicle, as well as the time, place and facts of the illegal act.
Article 19 Within five days after traffic technical monitoring equipment collects records of illegal acts, the public security organ traffic management department at the place where the illegal act occurred shall review the content of the records, and after review without error, enter them into the road traffic illegal act information management system as evidence for punishing illegal acts.
Article 20 On the same day that information on illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment is entered into the road traffic illegal act information management system, the public security organ traffic management departments at the place where the illegal act occurred and at the place where the motor vehicle is registered shall provide inquiries to the society. The public security organ traffic management department at the place where the illegal act occurred shall, within five days after the information on the illegal act is entered into the road traffic illegal act information management system, notify the person who committed the illegal act or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle of the time, place and facts of the illegal act through mobile internet applications, mobile phone text messages or mail, etc., according to the contact information in the motor vehicle filing information, and inform them to accept handling within thirty days.
The public security organ traffic management department shall, when the person who committed the illegal act or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle handles the illegal act and traffic accident, or handles motor vehicle or driver's license business, confirm in writing the contact information and legal document service method of the person who committed the illegal act or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle, and inform them that they may file or change the contact information and legal document service method through the internet website of the public security organ traffic management department, mobile internet applications, etc.
Article 21 For information on illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment, if the actual driver can be determined after verification, the public security organ traffic management department may record it in the road traffic illegal act information management system as illegal act information of the actual driver.
Article 22 Where information on illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment or entered into the road traffic illegal act information management system falls under any of the following circumstances and is verified, the public security organ traffic management department at the place where the illegal act occurred or at the place where the motor vehicle is registered shall eliminate it within three days from the date of verification:
(1) Illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment during the performance of emergency tasks by police vehicles, fire rescue vehicles, ambulances, and engineering rescue vehicles;
(2) Illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment during the period when the motor vehicle was stolen or robbed or the motor vehicle license plate was misused by others, as proven by a police report record provided by the owner or manager of the motor vehicle;
(3) Illegal acts caused by the motor vehicle rescuing from danger or emergency avoidance, as proven by evidence provided by the person who committed the illegal act or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle;
(4) Illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment that have been handled on the spot by traffic police;
(5) Illegal acts caused by inconsistent traffic signal indications;
(6) Records of illegal acts collected by traffic technical monitoring equipment used as the basis for handling that cannot clearly and accurately reflect the type, license plate, appearance and other characteristics of the motor vehicle, as well as the time, place and facts of the illegal act;
(7) Where, by comparing the photos of illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment with the motor vehicle information registered in the road traffic illegal act information management system, it is confirmed that the recorded motor vehicle license plate information is incorrect;
(8) Other circumstances that should be eliminated.
Article 23 After investigation and verification, photos or videos of illegal acts provided by units or individuals may be used as evidence for punishment.
The review and entry requirements for photos or video materials of illegal acts reported by the public shall be implemented with reference to these provisions.
Chapter 4 Application of Administrative Compulsory Measures
Article 24 Public security organ traffic management departments and their traffic police may, in accordance with the law, take the following administrative compulsory measures during law enforcement:
(1) Detention of vehicles;
(2) Detention of motor vehicle driver's licenses;
(3) Towing of motor vehicles;
(4) Testing the content of alcohol, state-controlled psychotropic drugs and narcotic drugs in the body;
(5) Confiscation of items;
(6) Other administrative compulsory measures prescribed by laws and regulations.
Article 25 The administrative compulsory measures under items (1), (2), (4) and (5) of Article 24 of these provisions shall be implemented in accordance with the following procedures:
(1) Orally inform the person who committed the illegal act or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle of the basic facts of the illegal act, the type, basis of the administrative compulsory measure to be taken, and the rights they enjoy according to law;
(2) Listen to the statements and defenses of the parties; if the facts, reasons or evidence put forward by the parties are established, they shall be adopted;
(3) Prepare a certificate of administrative compulsory measures, and inform the parties to go to the designated place for handling within fifteen days;
(4) The certificate of administrative compulsory measures shall be signed by the party and the traffic police or stamped, and affixed with the seal of the public security organ traffic management department; if the party refuses to sign, the traffic police shall note it on the certificate of administrative compulsory measures;
(5) The certificate of administrative compulsory measures shall be delivered to the party on the spot; if the party refuses to accept it, the traffic police shall note it on the certificate of administrative compulsory measures, which shall constitute service.
Where administrative compulsory measures are taken on the spot, the traffic police shall report to the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department to which they belong within twenty-four hours and complete the approval procedures. If the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department considers that administrative compulsory measures should not be taken, they shall be immediately lifted.
Article 26 The certificate of administrative compulsory measures shall state the basic information of the party, the vehicle license plate number, the vehicle type, the illegal facts, the type and basis of the administrative compulsory measure taken, the specific place and time limit for accepting handling, the name of the deciding organ and the cur

content such as administrative reconsideration and administrative litigation rights enjoyed by parties in accordance with the law.
Article 27: Vehicles shall be detained in accordance with the law under any of the following circumstances:
(1) A motor vehicle driving on the road fails to display a motor vehicle license plate, fails to place an inspection qualification mark or insurance mark, or fails to carry the motor vehicle driving license and driver's license with the vehicle;
(2) There is suspicion of forging, altering, or using forged or altered motor vehicle registration certificates, license plates, driving licenses, inspection qualification marks, insurance marks, or driver's licenses, or using the motor vehicle registration certificate, license plate, driving license, inspection qualification mark, or insurance mark of another vehicle;
(3) Compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles has not been purchased in accordance with state regulations;
(4) Highway passenger transport vehicles or freight motor vehicles are overloaded;
(5) There is suspicion that the motor vehicle is stolen or robbed;
(6) There is suspicion that the motor vehicle is assembled or has reached the scrapping standard;
(7) Highly toxic chemicals are transported by road without applying for a "Road Transport Permit for Highly Toxic Chemicals";
(8) A non-motor vehicle driver refuses to accept a fine penalty.
Where a road traffic accident occurs and it is necessary to collect evidence, the accident vehicle may be detained in accordance with the law.
Article 28: Traffic police shall, within twenty-four hours after detaining a vehicle, transfer the detained vehicle to the public security organ traffic management department to which they belong.
Where the public security organ traffic management department detains a vehicle, it shall not detain the cargo loaded on the vehicle. The party concerned shall be notified to handle the cargo loaded on the vehicle by themselves; if the party concerned is unable to handle it by themselves or fails to handle it by themselves, it shall be registered and properly kept. For items that are prone to rot, damage, loss, or other conditions not suitable for storage, upon approval by the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department at or above the county level, they may be sold or auctioned after photographing or video recording. The proceeds from the sale or auction shall be handled in accordance with relevant regulations.
Article 29: Where a highway passenger transport vehicle carries passengers exceeding the approved number of passengers, or a freight motor vehicle exceeds the approved load mass, the public security organ traffic management department shall eliminate the illegal state in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) If the violator can eliminate the illegal state by themselves, they shall, under the supervision of the public security organ traffic management department, transfer the excess passengers by themselves and unload the excess cargo;
(2) If the violator cannot eliminate the illegal state by themselves, for excess passengers, the public security organ traffic management department shall promptly notify relevant departments to contact and arrange transfer; for excess cargo, it shall be unloaded at a designated site, and the violator shall sign a custody contract for the unloaded cargo with the custodian of the designated site.
The costs of eliminating the illegal state shall be borne by the violator. After the illegal state is eliminated, the detained motor vehicle shall be returned immediately.
Article 30: For detained vehicles, after the party concerned accepts the handling or provides, supplements, and reissues relevant certificates or procedures which are verified, the public security organ traffic management department shall return them in accordance with the law in a timely manner.
The time for verification by the public security organ traffic management department shall not exceed ten days; if extension is needed, upon approval by the person in charge of the public security organ traffic management department at or above the county level, it may be extended to fifteen days. The verification time shall be calculated from the date when the vehicle driver or owner/manager provides proof of the legal origin of the detained vehicle, completes the corresponding procedures, or accepts the handling.
Where a vehicle is detained due to a road traffic accident for the purpose of collecting evidence, the detention period shall be implemented in accordance with the relevant provisions of the "Provisions on the Procedure for Handling Road Traffic Accidents".
Article 31: A motor vehicle driver's license shall be detained in accordance with the law under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Driving a motor vehicle after drinking alcohol;
(2) Entrusting a motor vehicle to a person who has not obtained a motor vehicle driver's license or whose motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked or temporarily suspended to drive;
(3) The motor vehicle travels at a speed exceeding the prescribed speed by more than fifty percent;
(4) Driving a motor vehicle suspected of being assembled or reaching the scrapping standard on the road;
(5) Accumulated points reach twelve within one scoring cycle.
Article 32: Traffic police shall, within twenty-four hours after detaining a motor vehicle driver's license, transfer the detained motor vehicle driver's license to the public security organ traffic management department to which they belong.
Where any of the circumstances listed in Items (1), (2), (3), and (4) of Article 31 of these Provisions exists, the motor vehicle driver's license shall be detained until the date the penalty decision is made; if the motor vehicle driver's license is detained before the penalty decision takes effect, one day of detention shall offset one day of the temporary suspension period. If only a fine penalty is imposed on the violator, the motor vehicle driver's license shall be returned immediately after the fine is paid. Where the circumstance listed in Item (5) of Article 31 of these Provisions exists, the motor vehicle driver's license shall be detained until the date the examination is passed.
Article 33: Where a driver violates the provisions on parking or temporary stopping of motor vehicles, and the driver is not at the scene or, although at the scene, refuses to leave immediately, thereby obstructing the passage of other vehicles or pedestrians, the public security organ traffic management department and its traffic police may tow the motor vehicle to a location that does not obstruct traffic or to a location designated by the public security organ traffic management department.
When towing a motor vehicle, the traffic police at the scene shall fix the illegal facts and evidence through methods such as photographing and video recording.
Article 34: The public security organ traffic management department shall make public the inquiry telephone number for towed motor vehicles, and shall inform the parties concerned by setting up special signboards for towed motor vehicles or by other means. The parties concerned may inquire by telephone about the location, time limit for handling, and the parking location of the towed motor vehicle.
Article 35: Where a vehicle driver has any of the following circumstances, the alcohol content in their body shall be tested:
(1) They object to the alcohol content result tested by methods such as alcohol breath test and raise the objection on the spot;
(2) A traffic accident occurs involving a vehicle suspected of driving after drinking alcohol;
(3) They are suspected of drunk driving;
(4) They refuse to cooperate with the alcohol breath test or other testing methods.
