Article 45 The penalty decision made under the simplified procedure shall state the basic information of the punished person, vehicle license plate number, vehicle type, illegal facts, basis for penalty, content of penalty, method of performance, time limit, name of the penalty authority, and the rights of administrative reconsideration and administrative litigation enjoyed by the punished person according to law, etc.

Article 46 The issuance of a Notice of Handling Illegal Acts shall be implemented according to the following procedures:
(1) Orally inform the illegal actor of the basic facts of the illegal act;
(2) Listen to the statement and defense of the illegal actor; if the facts, reasons, or evidence put forward by the illegal actor are established, they shall be adopted;
(3) Prepare the Notice of Handling Illegal Acts and notify the party to accept handling within fifteen days;
(4) The Notice of Handling Illegal Acts shall be signed by the illegal actor, signed or sealed by the traffic police officer, and affixed with the seal of the public security organ traffic management department; if the party refuses to sign, the traffic police officer shall note it on the Notice of Handling Illegal Acts;
(5) The Notice of Handling Illegal Acts shall be delivered to the party on the spot; if the party refuses to accept it, the traffic police officer shall note it on the Notice of Handling Illegal Acts, which shall constitute service.

The traffic police officer shall report the Notice of Handling Illegal Acts to the public security organ traffic management department to which they belong for the record within twenty-four hours.

Article 47 The Notice of Handling Illegal Acts shall state the basic information of the party, vehicle license plate number, vehicle type, illegal facts, specific location and time limit for accepting handling, name of the notifying authority, etc.

Article 48 Where a penalty decision is made under the general procedure, it shall be implemented by two or more traffic police officers according to the following procedures:
(1) Investigate the illegal facts, inquire of the party regarding the basic circumstances of the illegal act, and prepare a record of inquiry; if the party refuses to accept inquiry, sign, or affix a seal, the traffic police officer shall note it on the record of inquiry;
(2) Inform the party in writing or in the form of a record of the facts, reasons, and basis of the proposed administrative penalty, and inform them of the rights they enjoy according to law;
(3) Review and verify the statement and defense of the party, and the results of the review shall be noted in the record;
(4) Prepare the administrative penalty decision;
(5) The administrative penalty decision shall be signed by the punished person and affixed with the seal of the public security organ traffic management department; if the punished person refuses to sign, the traffic police officer shall note it on the penalty decision;
(6) The administrative penalty decision shall be delivered to the punished person on the spot; if the punished person refuses to accept it, the traffic police officer shall note it on the penalty decision, which shall constitute service; if the punished person is not present, it shall be served in accordance with the relevant provisions of the "Provisions of Public Security Organs on Handling Administrative Cases".

Article 49 The administrative penalty decision shall state the basic information of the punished person, vehicle license plate number, vehicle type, illegal facts and evidence, basis for penalty, content of penalty, method of performance, time limit, name of the penalty authority, and the rights of administrative reconsideration and administrative litigation enjoyed by the punished person according to law, etc.

Article 50 Where one person has two or more illegal acts, which are adjudicated separately and executed jointly, one administrative penalty decision may be prepared.

Where one person has only one illegal act and shall be subject to two or more types of penalties according to law, involving two penalty authorities, separate administrative penalty decisions shall be prepared.

Article 51 Where the facts of an illegal act are clear and a fine is to be imposed under the general procedure, the penalty decision shall be made within twenty-four hours from the time the illegal actor accepts handling; where the temporary suspension of a motor vehicle driver's license is imposed, the penalty decision shall be made within three days from the date the illegal actor accepts handling; where the revocation of a motor vehicle driver's license is imposed, the penalty decision shall be made within seven days from the date the illegal actor accepts handling or the hearing procedure ends; if a traffic accident constitutes a crime, the penalty decision shall be made in a timely manner after the judgment of the People's Court.

Article 52 For illegal acts recorded by traffic technical monitoring equipment, the party shall accept handling at the public security organ traffic management department in a timely manner; where a warning or a fine of not more than 200 yuan is imposed, the simplified procedure may apply; where a fine of more than 200 yuan (excluding 200 yuan) is imposed or the motor vehicle driver's license is revoked, the general procedure shall apply.

Article 53 After receiving the notice of road traffic safety illegal acts, the illegal actor or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle shall accept handling at the public security organ traffic management department in a timely manner. Where the owner or manager of a motor vehicle entrusts the motor vehicle to another person to drive, they shall notify the motor vehicle driver to accept handling within the time limit prescribed in Article 20 of these Provisions.

Where the illegal actor or the owner or manager of the motor vehicle is unable to accept handling within thirty days, they may apply for an extension of the handling period. The extended period shall not exceed three months at most.

